# issue #1150: Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true system-wide, so a clone
# of the template arrives with CRLF line endings while the update manifest
# hashes LF content (hundreds of files read as "modified"; bash scripts with
# CRLF break). Pin LF in the working tree; binaries are auto-detected.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
